 xmlns:trans="http://docbook.org/ns/transclusion">
  <info>
    <meta name="maintainer" content="amrita.sakthivel@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
    <title>Converting DM-RAID to MD-RAID</title>
    <abstract>
<para>
To migrate from dmraid (fakeRAID/ATA RAID) to mdadm (Linux Software RAID), you must first destroy the existing <literal>dmraid</literal> array and then create a new <literal>mdadm</literal> array.
</para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <procedure>
<title>Converting DM-RAID to MD-RAID</title>
<step><para>Unmount active file systems and deactivate the old mapper array (DM-RAID):</para>
<screen>&prompt.sudo; umount /dev/mapper/isw_*
  dmraid -an</screen>
</step>
<step><para>Switch Array to MD-RAID:</para>
  <substeps>
  <step><para>Option A (Intel IMSM / DDF FakeRAID — Keep Data):</para>
<screen>&prompt.sudo; mdadm --assemble --scan</screen>
  </step>
  <step><para>Option B (Fresh Native Linux RAID — Re-create):</para>
<screen>&prompt.sudo; dmraid -E -p /dev/sda /dev/sdb
mdadm --create /dev/md0 --level=1 --raid-devices=2 /dev/sda /dev/sdb
</screen>
      </step>
  </substeps>
  </step>
  <step><para>Save the new array configuration and grab its UUID to update <filename>/etc/fstab</filename> :</para>
<screen>&prompt.sudo; mdadm --detail --scan --verbose &gt;&gt; /etc/mdadm.conf
blkid /dev/md0</screen>
      <para>Edit <filename>/etc/fstab</filename> to replace old <filename>/dev/mapper/...</filename> entries with <filename>/dev/md0</filename> or the new <literal>UUID=..</literal>.</para>
    </step>
    <step><para>Regenerate dracut initramfs to load <literal>mdadm</literal> at boot and then update GRUB2:</para>
<screen>&prompt.sudo; dracut --force --regenerate-all
grub2-mkconfig -o /boot/grub2/grub.cfg</screen>
      </step>
      <step><para>Check that the array is active and syncing, then reboot:</para>
 <screen>&prompt.sudo; cat /proc/mdstat
  reboot</screen>
        </step>
  </procedure>
    </topic>